WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.072
Usage data: the Anthropic Economic Index.

2
00:00:03.352 --> 00:00:15.832
Anthropic publishes an Economic Index based on privacy-preserving analysis of Claude conversations, where another Claude instance classifies transcripts and only aggregates leave the analysis.

3
00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:19.163
Two 2026 reports are worth knowing.

4
00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:35.635
“Economic primitives” (15 January 2026), using about two million conversations from November 2025, introduced five measures: task complexity, required skills, use case, AI autonomy, and task success.

5
00:00:35.915 --> 00:00:36.811
On Claude.

6
00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:49.571
ai, augmentation (working with Claude) slightly exceeded automation (delegating to it), 52% to 45%, while API traffic was roughly three-quarters automation.

7
00:00:49.851 --> 00:00:54.224
Claude’s own assessment of task success was 67% on Claude.

8
00:00:54.504 --> 00:00:57.619
ai and 49% for API transcripts.

9
00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:08.565
The report estimated large speedups on complex tasks and, from them, a range of possible contributions to US labor productivity growth, roughly 1 to 1.

10
00:01:08.845 --> 00:01:11.832
8 percentage points a year in its main scenarios.

11
00:01:12.112 --> 00:01:20.133
“Cadences” (26 June 2026) paired usage data with a survey of about 9,700 users.

12
00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:32.808
Over a third expected AI to handle most of their tasks within a year, about 10% rated losing their own job as likely, and large majorities self-reported gains in speed and scope.

13
00:01:33.088 --> 00:01:49.472
Both reports list their limitations clearly, and they are the right model for how a provider should publish: classifiers are directional, task success is self-assessed and reflects which tasks users chose, the survey is not representative, and the measures are correlational.

14
00:01:49.752 --> 00:01:52.931
Use the Index to understand what people do with these tools.

15
00:01:53.211 --> 00:01:57.477
Do not use it as evidence of what the tools cause, and note who publishes it.
